  "verbalization": "D-Glutamic Acid appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the Fibrinogen beta chain, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that D-Glutamic Acid acts as a target for D-Aspartic Acid, which in turn targets Fibrinogen beta chain through various pathways. One pathway involves D-Aspartic Acid directly targeting Fibrinogen beta chain, while another involves D-Glutamic Acid targeting 5-oxoprolinase, which is then targeted by D-Aspartic Acid. This suggests a potential role for D-Glutamic Acid in modulating the activity of D-Aspartic Acid, which may influence the production or function of Fibrinogen beta chain. The presence of multiple indirect pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, but the consistent involvement of D-Aspartic Acid as a mediator supports a unified mechanism. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of D-Aspartic Acid in linking D-Glutamic Acid to Fibrinogen beta chain, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
